We have{
(\sqrt{7} + \sqrt{5})^6 &= (\sqrt{7} + \sqrt{5})^2 \cdot (\sqrt{7} + \sqrt{5})^2 \\
&= (\sqrt{7} + \sqrt{5})^2 \cdot (\sqrt{7} + \sqrt{5})^2 \\
&= 12 \cdot 12 \\
&= 144.
}So, the greatest integer less than 144 is $\boxed{143}$.Answer: 143
